{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_019ZZbjoYS8RgxxNZzVaGE4Z","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t//\n2\t//  CircularBuffer.h\n3\t//\n4\t//  Created by 罗亮富(Roen)zxllf23@163.com on 14-1-14.\n5\t//  Copyright (c) 2014年 All rights reserved.\n6\t//\n7\t\n8\t#ifndef YYDJ_Roen_CircularBuffer_h\n9\t#define YYDJ_Roen_CircularBuffer_h\n10\t#include <stdio.h>\n11\t#include <stdlib.h>\n12\t#include <stdbool.h>\n13\t\n14\t/*\n15\t A circular buffer(circular queue, cyclic buffer or ring buffer), is a data structure that uses a single, fixed-size buffer as if it were connected end-to-end. This structure lends itself easily to buffering data streams. visit https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Circular_buffer to see more information.\n16\t */\n17\t\n18\ttypedef struct s_circularBuffer* CircularBuffer;\n19\t\n20\t// Construct CircularBuffer with ‘size' in byte. You must call CircularBufferFree() in balance for destruction.\n21\textern CircularBuffer CircularBufferCreate(size_t size);\n22\t\n23\t// Destruct CircularBuffer \n24\textern void CircularBufferFree(CircularBuffer cBuf);\n25\t\n26\t// Reset the CircularBuffer\n27\textern void CircularBufferReset(CircularBuffer cBuf);\n28\t\n29\t//get the capacity of CircularBuffer\n30\textern size_t CircularBufferGetCapacity(CircularBuffer cBuf);\n31\t\n32\t//same as CircularBufferGetCapacity, Just for compatibility with older versions\n33\textern size_t CircularBufferGetSize(CircularBuffer cBuf);\n34\t\n35\t//get occupied data size of CircularBuffer\n36\textern size_t CircularBufferGetDataSize(CircularBuffer cBuf);\n37\t\n38\t// Push data to the tail of a circular buffer from 'src' with 'length' size in byte.\n39\textern void CircularBufferPush(CircularBuffer cBuf,void *src, size_t length);\n40\t\n41\t// Pop data from a circular buffer to 'dataOut'  with wished 'length' size in byte,return the actual data size in byte popped out,which is less or equal to the input 'length parameter.\n42\textern size_t CircularBufferPop(CircularBuffer cBuf, size_t length, void *dataOut);\n43\t\n44\t// Read data from a circular buffer to 'dataOut'  with wished 'length' size in byte,return the actual data size in byte popped out,which is less or equal to the input 'length parameter.\n45\textern size_t CircularBufferRead(CircularBuffer cBuf, size_t length, void *dataOut);\n46\t\n47\t//for test purpose, print the circular buffer's data content by printf(...); the 'hex' parameters indicates that if the data should be printed in asscii string or hex data format.\n48\textern void CircularBufferPrint(CircularBuffer cBuf, bool hex);\n49\t\n50\t#endif\n51\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b503c411-93f0-408f-9fa6-e7864a835b28","uuid":"4a408479-0a49-492b-8110-d7eeb26f180a","timestamp":"2026-05-29T08:04:08.291Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/harvest-crust-zILwap/project/c_src/src/circular_buffer.h","content":"//\n//  CircularBuffer.h\n//\n//  Created by 罗亮富(Roen)zxllf23@163.com on 14-1-14.\n//  Copyright (c) 2014年 All rights reserved.\n//\n\n#ifndef YYDJ_Roen_CircularBuffer_h\n#define YYDJ_Roen_CircularBuffer_h\n#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n#include <stdbool.h>\n\n/*\n A circular buffer(circular queue, cyclic buffer or ring buffer), is a data structure that uses a single, fixed-size buffer as if it were connected end-to-end. This structure lends itself easily to buffering data streams. visit https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Circular_buffer to see more information.\n */\n\ntypedef struct s_circularBuffer* CircularBuffer;\n\n// Construct CircularBuffer with ‘size' in byte. You must call CircularBufferFree() in balance for destruction.\nextern CircularBuffer CircularBufferCreate(size_t size);\n\n// Destruct CircularBuffer \nextern void CircularBufferFree(CircularBuffer cBuf);\n\n// Reset the CircularBuffer\nextern void CircularBufferReset(CircularBuffer cBuf);\n\n//get the capacity of CircularBuffer\nextern size_t CircularBufferGetCapacity(CircularBuffer cBuf);\n\n//same as CircularBufferGetCapacity, Just for compatibility with older versions\nextern size_t CircularBufferGetSize(CircularBuffer cBuf);\n\n//get occupied data size of CircularBuffer\nextern size_t CircularBufferGetDataSize(CircularBuffer cBuf);\n\n// Push data to the tail of a circular buffer from 'src' with 'length' size in byte.\nextern void CircularBufferPush(CircularBuffer cBuf,void *src, size_t length);\n\n// Pop data from a circular buffer to 'dataOut'  with wished 'length' size in byte,return the actual data size in byte popped out,which is less or equal to the input 'length parameter.\nextern size_t CircularBufferPop(CircularBuffer cBuf, size_t length, void *dataOut);\n\n// Read data from a circular buffer to 'dataOut'  with wished 'length' size in byte,return the actual data size in byte popped out,which is less or equal to the input 'length parameter.\nextern size_t CircularBufferRead(CircularBuffer cBuf, size_t length, void *dataOut);\n\n//for test purpose, print the circular buffer's data content by printf(...); the 'hex' parameters indicates that if the data should be printed in asscii string or hex data format.\nextern void CircularBufferPrint(CircularBuffer cBuf, bool hex);\n\n#endif\n","numLines":51,"startLine":1,"totalLines":51}}}
